(4574569, 657504, 79021, '<td valign="top">This would be my pick for a blue, definitely should ribbon.  The composition is perfect with the worker to the right of the frame, revealing the garbage behind him.  The lighting on the face is extremely well done.  The grainy gray sky adds a more to the feel of pollution, which works very well... based on lighting, composition, subject, processing, and originality, you get probably my only 10</td>', 'This would be my pick for a blue, definitely should ribbon.  The composition is perfect with the worker to the right of the frame, revealing the garbage behind him.  The lighting on the face is extremely well done.  The grainy gray sky adds a more to the feel of pollution, which works very well... based on lighting, composition, subject, processing, and originality, you get probably my only 10', '2008-03-19 15:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574572, 659235, 79021, '<td valign="top">out of focus bird, slightly out of focus person.  Looks like a typical snapshot at a zoo...2</td>', 'out of focus bird, slightly out of focus person.  Looks like a typical snapshot at a zoo...2', '2008-03-19 15:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574577, 658687, 79021, '<td valign="top">It doesn''t look like the child is very happy to be photographed.  You can''t tell it is a car seat without the title, perhaps zooming out some would help that.  Lighting is flat and overall the picture just looks like a snapshot of a kid...2</td>', 'It doesn''t look like the child is very happy to be photographed.  You can''t tell it is a car seat without the title, perhaps zooming out some would help that.  Lighting is flat and overall the picture just looks like a snapshot of a kid...2', '2008-03-19 15:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574584, 659666, 79021, '<td valign="top">This "dave hill" type technique does not always work, and I think this is a case where a potentially good and interesting shot is ruined by trying out that kind of processing.  The processing on the face makes him look somewhat ill.  Take the original and process it again with a more natural look, rather than the plastic type look... 3</td>', 'This "dave hill" type technique does not always work, and I think this is a case where a potentially good and interesting shot is ruined by trying out that kind of processing.  The processing on the face makes him look somewhat ill.  Take the original and process it again with a more natural look, rather than the plastic type look... 3', '2008-03-19 15:53:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574593, 658115, 79021, '<td valign="top">Cute kid dressed up at the beach during sunset.  Composition wise, I would have liked to see less sand or dirt and more water and sky.  Perhaps moving the kid back towards the edge (depending how high up you were) would help that.  Also, you have the sun and the child on the left and nothing on the right.  I would have preferred to have the child on the right side so that there is less empty space.  Finally, the child has no lighting on him.  A pop up flash for fill probably would have benefitted this, but a real flash, possibly an umbrella as well could have made this a more dramatic shot...4</td>', 'Cute kid dressed up at the beach during sunset.  Composition wise, I would have liked to see less sand or dirt and more water and sky.  Perhaps moving the kid back towards the edge (depending how high up you were) would help that.  Also, you have the sun and the child on the left and nothing on the right.  I would have preferred to have the child on the right side so that there is less empty space.  Finally, the child has no lighting on him.  A pop up flash for fill probably would have benefitted this, but a real flash, possibly an umbrella as well could have made this a more dramatic shot...4', '2008-03-19 15:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574606, 657185, 79021, '<td valign="top">His passion is jumping in weird poses in the snow with no shoes on?  It just doesn''t make sense to me.  Also, it seems odd that he is well lit but there is no foreground lighting or and light hitting the trees.  Makes for an odd combination, almost like he is cut and pasted from another picture...3</td>', 'His passion is jumping in weird poses in the snow with no shoes on?  It just doesn''t make sense to me.  Also, it seems odd that he is well lit but there is no foreground lighting or and light hitting the trees.  Makes for an odd combination, almost like he is cut and pasted from another picture...3', '2008-03-19 15:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574618, 659470, 79021, '<td valign="top">He is a case where the "dave hill" type look actually works.  The exaggerated colors of the sky and houses work well with his black suite.  The processing and the composition is well done, although, either the photo needs to be rotated slightly or there is some barrel distortion in the lens.  My only other gripe is that the shadow from his helmut almost doesn''t make his face visible.  However, the more I look at it and connect it to the title , I think that shadow might work, as it makes it as though this could be just a generic cop...either way, this gets a 7 from me</td>', 'He is a case where the "dave hill" type look actually works.  The exaggerated colors of the sky and houses work well with his black suite.  The processing and the composition is well done, although, either the photo needs to be rotated slightly or there is some barrel distortion in the lens.  My only other gripe is that the shadow from his helmut almost doesn''t make his face visible.  However, the more I look at it and connect it to the title , I think that shadow might work, as it makes it as though this could be just a generic cop...either way, this gets a 7 from me', '2008-03-19 16:03:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4574629, 659483, 19572, '<td valign="top">I like the sense of movement on the background.  the subject looks slightly out of focus to me...a bit sharper would have grabbed me more.</td>', 'I like the sense of movement on the background.  the subject looks slightly out of focus to me...a bit sharper would have grabbed me more.', '2008-03-19 16:05:56.000000', NULL, 1),
